 "about": "Black locust, green ash, Siberian and field elm and pedunculate oak in the shelterbelts and at the village edges; pedunculate, grey, downy and Turkey oak with field maple, silver lime and ash in the forest-steppe woods of Dobruja, Moldova and the river slopes; sessile oak, hornbeam and oriental beech on the Stavropol upland; white willow, black and white poplar and narrow-leaved ash in the floodplains and the Danube delta, Lombardy poplars along the roads, lone wild pears on the pastures, black and Scots pine planted on the sands; blackthorn, Tatar maple, hawthorn, dog rose, Christ's thorn and dwarf almond scrub on the steppe slopes, grey willow in the marshes; feather grass, fescue and Austrian wormwood on the steppe, reed in the limans and the delta; wheat, sunflower and maize fields, vineyards in Dobruja, Moldova and the Budjak; flocks of Tsigai, Karakul and merino sheep, village herds of spotted cattle, horses and goats; low whitewashed village houses, log houses in Bashkortostan, Orenburg and Samara. Hawthorn stands in for the fruit orchards.",
